      "prompt_html": "<p></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"../cambridge-ielts-1-13-tests/index.html\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Cambridge IELTS Tests 1 to 17</strong></a></p><p><strong><u>Task 1:</u></strong> The table below shows the proportion of different categories of families living in poverty in Australia in 1999.</p><p></p><p></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p><p></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.</p><p></p><p></p><figure><table><thead><tr><th>Family type</th><th data-align=\"center\">Proportion of people from each household type living in poverty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Single aged person</td><td data-align=\"center\">6% (54,000)</td></tr><tr><td>Aged couple</td><td data-align=\"center\">4% (48,000)</td></tr><tr><td>Single no children</td><td data-align=\"center\">19% (359,000)</td></tr><tr><td>Couple no children</td><td data-align=\"center\">7% (211,000)</td></tr><tr><td>Sole parent</td><td data-align=\"center\">21% (232,000)</td></tr><tr><td>Couple with children</td><td data-align=\"center\">12% (933,000)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>All households</strong></td><td data-align=\"center\"><strong>11% (1,837,000)</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p></p><p></p><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><br/><br/><ins data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-5700321813195736\" data-ad-format=\"auto\" data-ad-slot=\"5680584161\" data-full-width-responsive=\"true\" style=\"display: block;\"></ins><br/></p><p></p><p></p>",
